pssssst PRIMES
pssssst Trial division, then a lunge to collect every prime up to twenty.
pssssst Horses have moods: run with CLIPCLOP_CALM=1 to see what was supposed to happen.

pssssst Does any number from d down to 2 divide n?
pssssst (A whinny inside a whinny needs brackets, or the outer one loses its nicker.)
the Appaloosa divisible ridden by SingularHorse n and SingularHorse d says \
  whinny d \
    snort cl1p says neigh stomp \
    nicker says (whinny n % d \
      snort cl0p says neighneigh stomp \
      nicker says giddyup divisible with n and d - cl1p)

pssssst 0 has no stomp, so it falls through into 1's answer.
the Appaloosa prime ridden by SingularHorse n says \
  whinny n \
    snort cl0p says neigh \
    snort cl1p says neigh stomp \
    nicker says !(giddyup divisible with n and n - cl1p)

giddyup prime with cl1pcl1pcl1p
giddyup prime with cl1pcl0pcl0pcl1p

pssssst A lunge only counts down, and uses its horse up. Counting down is just
pssssst what we want here: each prime goes on the front, so the herd ends up in order.
the SingularHorse n says cl1pcl0pcl1pcl0pcl0p
the Herd primes says paddock
lunge n \
  the Herd primes says whinny (giddyup prime with n) \
    snort neighneigh says (herd of n) ++ primes stomp \
    nicker says primes \
whoa

pssssst 2 3 5 7 11 13 17 19
primes
pssssst n has been used up
n
